msgid "Moon Tokens"
msgstr ""

msgid "This campaign introduces a new kind of chaos token: The moon ([moon]) token. During the Circus Ex Mortis campaign, the moon plays a significant role, and the moon token represents both the strength and severity of its strange influence."
msgstr ""

msgid "[moon] tokens revealed during a skill test have the following effect: \"O. Seal this token on your investigator card and reveal another token.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "[moon] tokens sealed on your investigator card have no effect on their own, but some card effects may reference whether or not there is a [moon] token sealed on your investigator card, or the number of [moon] tokens sealed on your investigator card."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At the end of the round, for each [moon] token sealed on your investigator card, you must (choose one):\n"
"- That token stays sealed on your investigator card.\n"
"- Take 1 dama or 1 horror. Then, release that token."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A [moon] token evealed outside of a skill test has no effect on its own\n"
"unless otherwise specified by a card effect."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Tarot Deck"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If investigators choose to use the Tarot Deck from the <i>Return to the Circle Undone</i> expansion, there is some thematic connection to the <i>Circus Ex Mortis</i> campaign. Investigators may choose to perform an 8-card Campaign Reading with these specific 8 cards, in this order:\n"
"Magician, Hermit, Strength, Chariot, Devil, Temperance, Sun, Moon"
msgstr ""
